Long story short, Andy had learned how to open the cabinets.

990
00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:20.620
I listened, laughed at her story, and waited.

991
00:48:21.180 --> 00:48:24.560
When she was finished, I blurted out, I'm pregnant!

992
00:48:25.060 --> 00:48:30.500
I vaguely remember a thud and shrieking, and then after an epic bear hug, Jenna yelled,

993
00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:33.520
Why did you let me go on and on about my cat?

994
00:48:34.500 --> 00:48:37.560
This is accurate, but let me explain the thud.

995
00:48:38.080 --> 00:48:41.980
I had been sent to lunch early because we were shooting something that didn't involve

996
00:48:41.980 --> 00:48:42.760
front reception.

997
00:48:43.160 --> 00:48:47.560
By the time Angela got to my trailer, I was finished eating and had gotten up to do some

998
00:48:47.560 --> 00:48:48.100
exercise.

999
00:48:48.860 --> 00:48:54.200
I kept five-pound weights in my trailer and would do bicep curls or push-ups from time to time and

1000
00:48:54.200 --> 00:48:55.060
called out a workout.

1001
00:48:55.060 --> 00:48:56.960
I was trying, okay?

1002
00:48:57.780 --> 00:49:02.540
So I was pumping iron and droning on about my cat as Angela listened patiently.

1003
00:49:03.080 --> 00:49:05.800
Mid-curl, she told me she was pregnant.

1004
00:49:05.800 --> 00:49:11.760
I dropped the weights to the ground, causing the loud thud, then screamed for joy and hugged

1005
00:49:11.760 --> 00:49:12.600
my best friend.

1006
00:49:13.120 --> 00:49:16.540
Our production assistant knocked on the door to ask if everything was okay.

1007
00:49:17.220 --> 00:49:17.780
Yes!

1008
00:49:17.980 --> 00:49:19.900
We yelled through our tears of joy.

1009
00:49:20.520 --> 00:49:23.520
I knew how very much Angela wanted a child.

1010
00:49:23.840 --> 00:49:25.760
I knew she would make a wonderful mother.

1011
00:49:26.200 --> 00:49:28.020
I was just so happy for her.

1012
00:49:29.120 --> 00:49:33.540
In the weeks ahead, I shared the news with the rest of the cast, crew, and writing staff.

1013
00:49:33.940 --> 00:49:35.500
Everyone was so excited.

1014
00:49:35.800 --> 00:49:40.560
The writers started discussing how they might work the pregnancy into the show and what that

1015
00:49:40.560 --> 00:49:41.900
might mean for Angela Martin.

1016
00:49:42.460 --> 00:49:44.640
Then, something crazy happened.

1017
00:49:45.060 --> 00:49:50.540
The entire television and movie-making industry shut down due to the writers' strike, and

1018
00:49:50.540 --> 00:49:51.800
our show went on hiatus.

1019
00:49:52.440 --> 00:49:55.040
No one knew how long the writers' strike would laSt.

1020
00:49:55.280 --> 00:49:58.960
We had already filmed the first part of season four, and I wasn't showing then.

1021
00:49:59.480 --> 00:50:05.240
When we finally started production again, four months later, I was seven months pregnant.

1022
00:50:05.800 --> 00:50:08.760
I had a very obvious, very huge belly.

1023
00:50:10.220 --> 00:50:14.740
The characters and storylines of the show were meant to pick up right where we'd left off.

1024
00:50:15.000 --> 00:50:18.360
There was no way Angela's character could be pregnant out of the blue.

1025
00:50:18.880 --> 00:50:22.600
We knew we'd have to hide it, and for that, we had to get creative.

1026
00:50:23.540 --> 00:50:28.000
Angela did a lot of scenes standing behind the copier or the ficus plant in the bullpen.

1027
00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:31.720
My personal favorite belly hide was during dinner party.

1028
00:50:32.600 --> 00:50:36.180
Andy Bernard and Angela Martin arrive at Jan and Michael's party together.

1029
00:50:36.700 --> 00:50:41.180
The writers were puzzled as to how to disguise her pregnancy as they entered the condo.

1030
00:50:41.460 --> 00:50:43.560
There was no copier in Michael's apartment.

1031
00:50:44.200 --> 00:50:49.520
They came up with the idea of having Angela enter with a bouquet of flowers as a host gift.

1032
00:50:49.900 --> 00:50:51.060
Pam brings wine.

1033
00:50:51.400 --> 00:50:52.440
Angela brings flowers.

1034
00:50:52.820 --> 00:50:54.060
Problem solved, right?

1035
00:50:54.520 --> 00:50:55.260
Oh, no.

1036
00:50:55.940 --> 00:51:00.940
On the day of shooting, the prop team had to keep adding flowers to the bouquet until it was

1037
00:51:00.940 --> 00:51:01.740
enormous.

1038
00:51:02.060 --> 00:51:04.420
I mean, a truly ridiculous bouquet.

1039
00:51:04.860 --> 00:51:06.740
But that's how we hid the belly.

1040
00:51:07.900 --> 00:51:11.460
Angela was the first regular cast member to be pregnant on set.

1041
00:51:11.460 --> 00:51:14.620
So, it was as if we were all having that baby with her.

1042
00:51:15.360 --> 00:51:20.460
Everyone was so protective, making sure she got enough to eat, drank enough water, sat

1043
00:51:20.460 --> 00:51:21.500
down often enough.

1044
00:51:21.960 --> 00:51:25.880
The crew even threw her a surprise baby shower in the set parking lot.

1045
00:51:26.540 --> 00:51:31.360
At that same time, I teamed up with Angela's sister-in-law, Suzanne Daniels, and we threw

1046
00:51:31.360 --> 00:51:32.680
a friends and family shower.

1047
00:51:33.720 --> 00:51:37.960
Angela's mom, sisters, and grandmother all flew to Los Angeles for the event.

1048
00:51:38.940 --> 00:51:43.920
Celebrating Angela's pregnancy with this multi-generational group of women was moving to me.

1049
00:51:44.480 --> 00:51:49.580
These women, who had raised children of their own, were bringing Angela into the fold.

1050
00:51:49.980 --> 00:51:51.460
It was a beautiful thing.

1051
00:51:52.080 --> 00:51:57.260
At the same time, seeing Angela at her baby shower really drove home the fact that I was

1052
00:51:57.260 --> 00:51:59.280
very far away from joining that flock.

1053
00:52:00.600 --> 00:52:03.940
During the same month of the dual showers, Jenna was turning 34.

1054
00:52:04.560 --> 00:52:07.180
I wanted to be there for Jenna as her birthday approached.

1055
00:52:07.460 --> 00:52:08.920
She was doing so much for me.

1056
00:52:09.300 --> 00:52:13.520
But to illustrate the different directions our lives were taking, Jenna wanted to celebrate

1057
00:52:13.520 --> 00:52:16.620
her birthday at a bar in West Hollywood called St. Nick's.

1058
00:52:17.140 --> 00:52:20.780
It's no longer in business, but during its heyday, it was a great dive bar.

1059
00:52:21.120 --> 00:52:26.940
Dark interior, old pleather booths, a jukebox, the best greasy burgers, and a back room with

1060
00:52:26.940 --> 00:52:27.520
the dart board.

1061
00:52:28.220 --> 00:52:32.480
Imagine being eight months pregnant and walking into that bar holding

1062
00:52:32.480 --> 00:52:33.200
a sheet cake.

1063
00:52:33.760 --> 00:52:38.820
Yes, I brought Jenna a sheet cake from the grocery store, and then I waddled

1064
00:52:38.820 --> 00:52:41.120
to the back of the bar and ate half of it.

1065
00:52:42.060 --> 00:52:47.240
Angela, I will never forget looking over at you as you happily ate sheet cake and sang at

1066
00:52:47.240 --> 00:52:50.280
the top of your lungs to Lynyrd Skynyrd playing on the jukebox.

1067
00:52:50.540 --> 00:52:52.620
You were super pregnant, in

1068
00:52:52.620 --> 00:52:56.080
a dive bar, getting all kinds of side-eye from the other patrons.

1069
00:52:56.660 --> 00:52:58.460
You did that for me, and

1070
00:52:58.460 --> 00:52:59.400
I am forever grateful.

1071
00:53:02.780 --> 00:53:05.960
Well, that is our excerpt for this podcast episode.

1072
00:53:06.280 --> 00:53:08.360
This chapter was such a blast to

1073
00:53:08.360 --> 00:53:14.340
write, and we're so excited for you guys to read it or listen to it in the audiobook.

1074
00:53:14.700 --> 00:53:20.660
Speaking of audiobook, in case you missed it last week, we did a special feed drop, I guess

1075
00:53:20.660 --> 00:53:21.460
is what it's called.

1076
00:53:21.460 --> 00:53:27.060
We put the entire first chapter of our audiobook in the Office Ladies

1077
00:53:27.060 --> 00:53:29.100
podcast feed, so you can go listen to that.

1078
00:53:29.360 --> 00:53:32.000
Yeah, I'll put a swipe up in stories if you missed it.

1079
00:53:32.180 --> 00:53:33.860
But you guys, before we say goodbye

1080
00:53:33.860 --> 00:53:36.060
today, we have a few wrap-up questions.

1081
00:53:36.420 --> 00:53:39.440
The first one is from Jill in Marshfield, Ohio.

1082
00:53:40.180 --> 00:53:45.180
Jill says, obviously you're best friends, but how would you describe the dynamics of Lee

1083
00:53:45.180 --> 00:53:45.860
and Josh?

1084
00:53:46.480 --> 00:53:50.460
Sometimes best friends' spouses are amicable, but there are also times that

1085
00:53:50.460 --> 00:53:51.520
they just don't mesh.

1086
00:53:51.780 --> 00:53:53.360
I would say our fellas mesh.

1087
00:53:53.600 --> 00:53:54.440
So well.

1088
00:53:54.660 --> 00:53:54.980
Yes.

1089
00:53:55.200 --> 00:53:57.920
And I would say they got along, and they were friends.

1090
00:53:58.080 --> 00:53:59.740
We would do a lot of group activities

1091
00:53:59.740 --> 00:54:00.200
together.

1092
00:54:00.420 --> 00:54:05.360
Whenever we hang out with you guys, afterwards, Josh always says to me, Lee's so fun to be

1093
00:54:05.360 --> 00:54:05.700
around.

1094
00:54:05.900 --> 00:54:07.640
I gotta hang out with Lee more.

1095
00:54:07.820 --> 00:54:09.700
That's what Lee says about Josh.

1096
00:54:10.580 --> 00:54:12.060
But I will say one thing.

1097
00:54:13.020 --> 00:54:17.060
Nothing bonded these men like us writing this book.

1098
00:54:17.360 --> 00:54:17.800
Yeah.

1099
00:54:18.140 --> 00:54:23.680
Because they are the only two people on the planet who know what it was really like in

1100
00:54:23.680 --> 00:54:24.400
those trenches.

1101
00:54:25.140 --> 00:54:29.620
Jenna, when I showed Josh the book, he was like, oh my gosh, babe, it turned out so great.

1102
00:54:29.720 --> 00:54:30.700
He was so loving.

1103
00:54:30.880 --> 00:54:34.780
And we got to the dedication page, and he said, it should just say for Lee

1104
00:54:34.780 --> 00:54:35.340
and Josh.

1105
00:54:36.520 --> 00:54:38.240
Because we include our children.

1106
00:54:38.480 --> 00:54:40.520
And he's like, no, it should just say Lee and

1107
00:54:40.520 --> 00:54:40.780
Josh.

1108
00:54:41.300 --> 00:54:41.540
Yeah.

1109
00:54:41.920 --> 00:54:47.360
These guys did a lot of solo parenting on the weekends so that Angela and I could

1110
00:54:47.360 --> 00:54:47.640
write.

1111
00:54:47.840 --> 00:54:49.700
They made a lot of space for us.

1112
00:54:49.820 --> 00:54:51.160
They really stepped up.

1113
00:54:51.300 --> 00:54:52.800
They were wonderful partners

1114
00:54:52.800 --> 00:54:53.660
in this book.

1115
00:54:53.800 --> 00:54:55.660
I mean, it wouldn't be here without them, truly.

1116
00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:56.320
Truly.

1117
00:54:56.580 --> 00:54:57.700
And I will add this.

1118
00:54:58.240 --> 00:55:00.020
Lee is a phenomenal writer.

1119
00:55:00.300 --> 00:55:01.900
He is an amazing editor.

1120
00:55:02.180 --> 00:55:03.100
I can't tell

1121
00:55:03.100 --> 00:55:07.920
you how many times we took a chapter to him, and we were like, we think it's done.

1122
00:55:08.060 --> 00:55:08.580
We really

1123
00:55:08.580 --> 00:55:08.900
do.

1124
00:55:09.100 --> 00:55:10.500
Do you have any insight?

1125
00:55:10.680 --> 00:55:11.620
Do you have any advice?

1126
00:55:11.620 --> 00:55:12.480
We think it's done.

1127
00:55:12.600 --> 00:55:13.380
And he might have

1128
00:55:13.380 --> 00:55:18.840
one or two small suggestions that completely changed it and zhuzhed it in a way we couldn't

1129
00:55:18.840 --> 00:55:19.400
have thought of.

1130
00:55:19.580 --> 00:55:19.940
Yeah.

1131
00:55:20.040 --> 00:55:22.480
He did a lot of editing of this book, a lot of polishing.

1132
00:55:22.700 --> 00:55:23.680
I'm sure he's read it

1133
00:55:23.680 --> 00:55:25.200
dozens of times as well.

1134
00:55:25.300 --> 00:55:25.960
He has.

1135
00:55:26.120 --> 00:55:28.000
And here's my shout out for Josh.

1136
00:55:28.380 --> 00:55:30.260
Josh is just a technical wizard.

1137
00:55:30.740 --> 00:55:31.720
Here's an example.

1138
00:55:31.720 --> 00:55:37.900
We got the book back from Day Street from our publisher, and we wanted to be able to share

1139
00:55:37.900 --> 00:55:40.860
the document so we could work off one active document.

1140
00:55:41.440 --> 00:55:42.880
No one could seem to figure this

1141
00:55:42.880 --> 00:55:43.100
out.

1142
00:55:43.340 --> 00:55:43.960
Josh did it.

1143
00:55:44.140 --> 00:55:47.480
He made this living, breathing document that we could share in real time.

1144
00:55:47.660 --> 00:55:54.300
He also helped us recover some photos and memorabilia that I don't know if we could have included

1145
00:55:54.300 --> 00:55:56.700
in the book without his technical assistance.

1146
00:55:57.200 --> 00:56:01.420
Like, he helped us scan things and create a

1147
00:56:01.420 --> 00:56:03.020
resolution that was shareable.

1148
00:56:03.260 --> 00:56:06.040
And I mean, that just means so much to me.

1149
00:56:06.540 --> 00:56:12.200
So our fellows really came through for us, and I'm glad that we're giving them a shout out

1150
00:56:12.200 --> 00:56:12.720
here today.

1151
00:56:12.980 --> 00:56:13.180
Me too.

1152
00:56:13.600 --> 00:56:16.220
Well, our final question is from Megan G.

1153
00:56:16.420 --> 00:56:17.080
in Iowa.

1154
00:56:17.660 --> 00:56:20.080
What big takeaways do you want readers

1155
00:56:20.080 --> 00:56:25.200
to walk away with and any thoughts you want us to have before diving in?

1156
00:56:25.580 --> 00:56:26.740
Well, Megan, what

1157
00:56:26.740 --> 00:56:33.600
I would say is when you watch The Office, you're watching a group of people who are becoming good

1158
00:56:33.600 --> 00:56:34.220
friends.

1159
00:56:34.420 --> 00:56:36.900
And I mean the cast and the crew.

1160
00:56:37.340 --> 00:56:41.760
And what we hoped to convey in our book is that

1161
00:56:41.760 --> 00:56:44.460
intimacy of that group of people.

1162
00:56:44.460 --> 00:56:52.500
So we have a chapter about holiday episodes on The Office, but then we include all of the

1163
00:56:52.500 --> 00:56:59.220
ways that we celebrated the holidays off camera together because we're all real friends.

1164
00:56:59.760 --> 00:56:59.960
Yeah.

1165
00:57:00.120 --> 00:57:05.000
And I think also, Megan, this book for me is really about friendship.

1166
00:57:05.460 --> 00:57:06.520
It's the friends

1167
00:57:06.520 --> 00:57:12.420
we made on set, but it's also finding that friend in your life who builds you up and supports

1168
00:57:12.420 --> 00:57:17.060
you and is just this unwavering champion for you.

1169
00:57:17.160 --> 00:57:20.280
And I found that in Jenna, and I'm so thankful

1170
00:57:20.280 --> 00:57:20.880
for it.

1171
00:57:20.960 --> 00:57:26.960
And I hope our story of our friendship inspires people not to give up, you know, because

1172
00:57:26.960 --> 00:57:31.940
we didn't think we would make a friend this close and this meaningful in our 30s.

1173
00:57:32.320 --> 00:57:33.040
We thought

1174
00:57:33.040 --> 00:57:35.400
friendships were sort of things you make earlier in life.

1175
00:57:35.520 --> 00:57:37.200
And then by the time you're 30, you've

1176
00:57:37.200 --> 00:57:38.000
got all your friends.

1177
00:57:38.160 --> 00:57:39.520
But that's when we met.

1178
00:57:39.660 --> 00:57:41.940
And I would say, you just never know who's

1179
00:57:41.940 --> 00:57:45.760
going to come into your life and to leave that space and openness in your heart.

1180
00:57:46.300 --> 00:57:46.440
Yeah.

1181
00:57:46.920 --> 00:57:49.420
I mean, ultimately, this book is about friendship.

1182
00:57:49.740 --> 00:57:50.000
Yeah.

1183
00:57:50.560 --> 00:57:53.440
Well, guys, thank you so much.

1184
00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:55.680
We hope that you like the book.

1185
00:57:56.080 --> 00:57:58.240
It just came from our hearts

1186
00:57:58.240 --> 00:58:00.480
and we're really proud of it.

1187
00:58:00.600 --> 00:58:01.700
I'm sure you can tell.

1188
00:58:02.020 --> 00:58:03.580
Thanks for going on this journey

1189
00:58:03.580 --> 00:58:04.140
with us.

1190
00:58:04.140 --> 00:58:05.600
Thank you so much.

1191
00:58:05.760 --> 00:58:09.400
So many of you guys have sent in your questions and your comments and

1192
00:58:09.400 --> 00:58:13.500
your words of support really meant a lot to us over these years.

1193
00:58:13.700 --> 00:58:15.320
And we just can't thank you

1194
00:58:15.320 --> 00:58:15.700
enough.

1195
